&quot;text&quot;:&quot;&lt;p&gt;Click here for data point definitions&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;table class=\&quot;disclaimer-table laddered-buffer-disclaimer\&quot;&gt;
&lt;thead&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;th&gt;Data Point&lt;/th&gt;&lt;th&gt;Definition&lt;/th&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/thead&gt;
&lt;tbody&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tranche Start Date&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The start date of the Tranche.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tranche End Date&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The last day of the Tranche.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Initial Reference Asset Value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Price of the Reference Asset as of the close of market on the day before the Tranche Start Date.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tranche Cap Value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The price of the Reference Asset at which the Tranche Cap is reached. The Tranche Cap Value is based on the strike price of the written call options sold in connection with the Tranche. Note that the Fund may not write such call options when they provide limited to no economic value to the Fund and

column4216:
 the Tranche Cap may at times be greater than indicated.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Initial Tranche Cap Percentage&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The percentage increase in the Reference Asset Value (as of the Tranche Start Date) until the Tranche Cap Value is reached

column4217:
 determined as of the Tranche Start Date. This is the approximate upside limit for the Tranche. The Initial Tranche Cap Percentage is calculated as follows: (Tranche Cap Value – Reference Asset Value as of the Tranche Start Date) / Reference Asset Value as of the Tranche Start Date.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tranche Buffer Start Value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The price of the Reference Asset at which the downside protection from the Tranche Buffer starts. The Tranche Buffer Start Value is based on the strike price of the put options purchased in the set of FLEX Options included in the Tranche.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Initial Tranche Buffer Start Percentage&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The percentage reduction in the Reference Asset Value (as of the Tranche Start Date) before the downside protection from the Tranche Buffer starts

column4218:
 determined as of the Tranche Start Date. The Initial Tranche Buffer Start Percentage is calculated as follows: (Tranche Buffer Start Value – Reference Asset Value as of the Tranche Start Date) / Reference Asset Value as of the Tranche Start Date.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tranche Buffer End Value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The price of the Reference Asset at which the downside protection from the Tranche Buffer ends. The Tranche Buffer End Value is based on the strike price of the options written in the set of FLEX Options included in the Tranche.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Initial Tranche Buffer End Percentage&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The percentage reduction in the Reference Asset Value (as of the Tranche Start Date) before the Tranche reaches the Tranche Buffer End Value

column4220:
 determined as of the Tranche Start Date. The Initial Tranche Buffer End Percentage is calculated as follows: (Tranche Buffer End Value – Reference Asset Value as of the Outcome Tranche Start Date) / Reference Asset Value as of the Outcome Tranche Start Date.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Remaining Tranche Period&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The days remaining in a Tranche until the Tranche End Date.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Reference Asset Value&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The current price of the Reference Asset.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Remaining Tranche Cap Percentage&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The percentage change in the current Reference Asset Value until the Tranche Cap Value is reached and is the current approximate upside limit for the Tranche. The Remaining Tranche Cap Percentage is calculated as follows: (Tranche Cap Value – Reference Asset Value) / Reference Asset Value. On the Tranche Start Date

column4221:
 the Remaining Tranche Cap is the Initial Tranche Cap Percentage.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Reference Asset Value Change to Tranche Buffer Start&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The percentage change in the current Reference Asset Value until the price of the Reference Asset reaches the Tranche Buffer Start Value and provides downside protection until the Tranche Buffer End Value. The Reference Asset Value Change to Tranche Buffer Start is calculated as follows: (Tranche Buffer Start Value – Reference Asset Value) / Reference Asset Value. At the Tranche Start Date

column4222:
 this is the Initial Tranche Buffer Start Percentage.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Reference Asset Value Change to Tranche Buffer End&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The percentage change in the current Reference Asset Value until the price of the Reference Asset reaches the Tranche Buffer End Value. The Reference Asset Value Change to Tranche Buffer End is calculated as follows: (Tranche Buffer End Value – Reference Asset Value) / Reference Asset Value. At the Tranche Start Date

column4223:
 this is the Initial Tranche Buffer End Percentage.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;tr&gt;
&lt;td&gt;Tranche Weight of the Fund&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;td&gt;The approximate weight of the set of FLEX Options in the Tranche relative to the overall portfolio of the Fund.&lt;/td&gt;
&lt;/tr&gt;
&lt;/tbody&gt;
